vy Republican outside spending in the final days could tighten the race toward tossup territory.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Tony Evers (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Wisconsin's open governor's race pits Milwaukee County Executive David Crowley against Congressman Tom Tiffany after Tony Evers declined to seek reelection. Polling has consistently favored Crowley, with the final Marquette University survey showing a 7-point lead and averages across outlets clustering around a 4-5 point Democratic margin. Even polls sponsored by Republican-leaning firms show Crowley ahead.\n\nTiffany has out-raised Crowley by roughly ten to one and total spending has topped $166 million, a state record, giving Republicans a path if the electorate shifts. Most expert ratings call the race Lean D, though a couple rate it a Tossup, and prediction markets price Crowley as a strong favorite. The race remains competitive in a state that is evenly divided overall.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7127, "margin": 2.83}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7543, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7549, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7725, "margin": 3.8}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7589, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7208, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.724, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7645, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7536, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7419, "margin": 3.2}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.746, "margin": 3.2}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7525, "margin": 3.2}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7388, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.6631, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.6796, "margin": 2.7}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.6642, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.7316, "margin": 3.2}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.696, "margin": 3